ve in positive thinking so  i'm like it's not going to happen it's  not going to happen it's not going to  happen it's not going to happen  refuse to accept that it's a possibility  that this could happen  jamie is now focused on getting his  strength back  and while he's no longer in hospital  he's not far from the thoughts of those  who cared for him  kovid19 has left so many in healthcare  feeling drained and deflated jaime's  story  is something of a booster shot to know  that he actually  is home is miraculous  i think to us for this covet survivor  the miracle is a renewed positivity in  life  and another walk with yoland mike  drolite global news toronto  and that's global national for this  wednesday i'm donna friesen  tonight's your candidate is a couple of  moose exploring calgary's mackenzie lake  one took a dip in the lake and and why  not really  the place belongs to them besides  snacking on some gardens  residents say the wild visitors were  well behaved  love to jump in that lake myself thanks  for watching hope to see you here again  tomorrow  take care of yourselves bye-bye  [Music]  [Applause]  you
 

